.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt PAM_CAPABILITY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pam_capability
.Nd compatibility module for retired login capability grants
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
module is retained for locally modified PAM configurations surviving upgrades.
It does not authenticate, issue authority, modify discovery channels, or change
session attribution.
Its authentication hook returns
.Dv PAM_IGNORE ;
its credential and session hooks return success without taking action.
.Pp
New PAM configurations do not use this module.
Existing references may be removed while preserving the normal UNIX
authentication modules.
Software entitlements and authenticated user/session authority are independent
inputs to service authorization.
Successful PAM credential or session hooks in this compatibility module do not
establish either authority or enroll an authentication issuer.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pam.conf 5
